===== verdict on Rbar =====
  [T] definition: Rbar = C''(0)/C(0) = <m^2>_nu, mass^2 (ch05:426-428, ch02:12-13)
  [T] zero-cost exact: <1-e^-m> = 1-C1/C0 ; <m> >= -ln(C1/C0) ; Rbar >= <m>^2
  [T] DIRECTION: the bridge needs an UPPER bound on Rbar (Lstar > Rbar).  The
      zero-cost inequalities are LOWER bounds -> they only cap the headroom
      rho^2 - rbar, they cannot certify w1 > 0.
  [E] degeneracy test (Cauchy-Schwarz, exact): (C1/C0)^2 = 0.0151 <= C2/C0 = 0.0360 -> measure is NON-degenerate, so Rbar > <m>^2.
  [C] Rbar itself needs an ansatz (spectral reconstruction); no zero-cost value;
      the NNLS estimate grows without bound with the assumed UV end of the grid
      (Rbar = 6.8/10/20/52 for m_max = 3/4/6/10) -> Rbar is UV-dominated, i.e. a
      cutoff quantity, not an IR one.  No (L,a)-uniform premise can be built on it.
  [T] P8:39 ("time first moment / m_eff weighted") evaluates to <m>, a MASS;
      feeding it as Rbar divides by m1^2 without the extra power -> rbar too
      small -> w1 bound too large (column "w1(lin)"). It is NOT Rbar.
